    "message": {
      "content": "# Validation Checklist: Multi-Node Language-Model Serving System\n\n## Scope and Preconditions\n\nBefore running any checks, establish the test envelope:\n\n- [ ] **System topology documented**: number of nodes, GPUs/accelerators per node, interconnect (NVLink, InfiniBand, Ethernet), and serving architecture (tensor parallel, pipeline parallel, data parallel, expert parallel, or hybrid).\n- [ ] **Baseline defined**: a single-node or reference configuration whose outputs/latency serve as the comparison anchor.\n- [ ] **Test workloads frozen**: prompt sets, token counts, sampling parameters (temperature, top-p, seeds where supported), and concurrency levels are versioned and identical across all runs being compared.\n- [ ] **Environment captured**: driver versions, runtime versions (CUDA/ROCm), framework commit hashes, container image digests, and kernel versions recorded per node.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Configuration Identity\n\nGoal: prove that every node believes it is running the *same* system.\n\n- [ ] **Model artifact identity**: all nodes load the model from the same immutable source. Verify via checksum (SHA-256 of weights, or digest of the manifest), not just path/filename. A shared filesystem path is not proof of identity \u2014 verify content.\n- [ ] **Tokenizer identity**: tokenizer version/config hash identical across nodes. Mismatched tokenizers can produce silently divergent outputs even with identical weights.\n- [ ] **Config hash propagation**: compute a hash of the full serving configuration (parallelism degrees, quantization settings, KV-cache dtype, max sequence length, chunked prefill settings, scheduler policies) and confirm every rank/node reports the same hash at startup.\n- [ ] **Derived-config consistency**: check settings that are *computed* rather than copied \u2014 e.g., per-GPU memory fractions, derived block counts, effective batch limits. These should be consistent given identical inputs; divergence indicates environment drift (different VRAM, different visible devices).\n-",
      "reasoning": "",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
